{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "def find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(xs) % 2 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Coefficient count must be even to find a zero point.\")\n\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n    max_iterations = 1000\n    search_range_start = -5.0\n    search_range_end = 5.0\n    step_size = 0.01\n\n    # Check endpoints of the initial search range\n    if abs(poly(xs, search_range_start)) < tolerance:\n        return search_range_start\n    if abs(poly(xs, search_range_end)) < tolerance:\n        return search_range_end\n\n    a = search_range_start\n    f_a = poly(xs, a)\n\n    while a < search_range_end:\n        b = a + step_size\n        if b > search_range_end:\n            b = search_range_end\n        \n        f_b = poly(xs, b)\n\n        if abs(f_b) < tolerance:\n            return b\n\n        if f_a * f_b < 0:  # Found a sign change, apply bisection method\n            low = a\n            high = b\n            for _ in range(max_iterations):\n                mid = (low + high) / 2\n                f_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n                if abs(f_mid) < tolerance:\n                    return mid\n\n                if poly(xs, low) * f_mid < 0:\n                    high = mid\n                else:\n                    low = mid\n            return (low + high) / 2 # Return best estimate if max iterations reached\n\n        # Move to the next interval\n        a = b\n        f_a = f_b\n\n    raise ValueError(\"Could not find a zero point within the specified search range or tolerance.\")"}
