{"task_id": "HumanEval/43", "solution": "def pairs_sum_to_zero(l):\n    \"\"\"\n    pairs_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    it returns True if there are two distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    for num in l:\n        target = -num\n        if target in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(num)\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Converts an integer x to the specified base, returning its string representation. The base must be less than 10.\"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    result = []\n    is_negative = False\n    if x < 0:\n        is_negative = True\n        x = abs(x)\n\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        result.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n\n    if is_negative:\n        result.append('-')\n\n    return ''.join(result[::-1])"}
